INT. FAMILY COURT - CORRIDOR - DAY

A scuffed hallway with benches along both walls. A vending machine hums. Fluorescent light flattens every face.

On one bench: FERNANDO "FERN" ALCANTARA, 40s, in his only suit, and his lawyer, CORDELIA WASHINGTON-PRICE, 50s, flipping a file. On the opposite bench: BRONWEN ALCANTARA-HUGHES, 40s, his ex-wife, rigid, flanked by her attorney, ISAAC FELDSTEIN, 30s, and her sister, MARISELA TRUJILLO, 40s, who glares across the aisle.

                    CORDELIA
Fern. Look at me.

                    FERN
I'm looking.

                    CORDELIA
You say nothing in there. Understood?

                    FERN
Understood.

                    CORDELIA
Even if she provokes you.

                    FERN
She always provokes me.

                    CORDELIA
Then you say nothing twice.

Across the aisle, Marisela leans to whisper in Bronwen's ear. Bronwen shakes her head.

                    MARISELA
(loud)
He's a liar, Bron.

                    ISAAC
Marisela.

                    MARISELA
He is.

                    ISAAC
Please.

Fern stands, fists clenched. Cordelia seizes his sleeve. Marisela stands too. Isaac steps between them, hands out, and Bronwen rises last, pale, her palms pressed flat against her skirt.

                    FERN
She said that in front of my kids?

                    BRONWEN
Fern, sit down.

                    FERN
Don't tell me what to do, Bronwen.

                    BRONWEN
I'm asking.

                    FERN
You've never asked me anything in your life.

                    BRONWEN
I'm asking now.

He stops. Searches her face. The vending machine hums.

                    CORDELIA
(quietly)
Fern.

He sits. Slowly. Marisela sits too, sulking. Isaac exhales and returns to his folder.

The courtroom door opens. A BAILIFF leans out.

                    BAILIFF
Alcantara versus Alcantara-Hughes.

All five of them stand. They file toward the door, and in the narrow frame Fern and Bronwen end up shoulder to shoulder, neither willing to go first.

                    BRONWEN
After you.

                    FERN
No. After you.

Cordelia, behind them, rolls her eyes and shoves them both through the door.
